		{
			description: [
				"Suspicious blocks are fragile. Carry a brush while exploring ruins and avoid breaking the block before its item is revealed."
				"Brush suspicious blocks from a stable position and watch the emerging item. Falling blocks, water, hostile mobs, and careless mining can ruin the context even when the artifact itself survives."
				"Better Archeology expands suspicious sand and gravel into a broader field practice with fossils, ruins, artifact shards, and analysis. Bring several brushes, light, scaffolding blocks, and empty protected inventory slots."
				"The Curators' Compact keeps an original, a display example, and a replaceable field copy when possible. Rare knowledge belongs to the settlement even when the person who found it is offline."
			]
			id: "03AC335757DE4153"
